ond  fairy king thrown in for good measure  obviously it'll also matter how they  handle the fights and how satisfying  they are but the setup here has  so much potential what i also love to  see from the trailer is meliotis and  zeldris  fighting side by side they're two of my  favorite brothers in anime and i  love to see them on the same side this  time defending the demon world  in the first trailer we also saw king in  his king of rock form  merlin with her mouth covered so we  don't see the burn marks she got from  escanor in this first trailer and  king arthur will make an appearance too  as we see him  crying in the trailer but i do think the  main focus  is going to be on our seven deadly sins  which is exactly what we want from this  series  i'm more interested in the second  trailer though we get a better sense of  dahlia's powers  which seem to be fire based i've even  heard theories that he's inherited  sunshine but that's probably a stretch  at this point  it is in this trailer that will see the  supreme deity  and props to how they reveal the supreme  deity too unless you pause at the  perfect time  you will easily miss her since light  surrounds her as soon as she appears in  the trailer engulfing the whole screen  if you do pause it at just the right  time though you could see her with her  head covered in light as usual and we  see vaughn  king gother and diane confronting her  notably meliotis and elizabeth aren't  there but it's just one scene and they  may well get the chance to confront her  afterwards which is my hope  she is more so their personalized  villain anyways so i think it would be  more satisfying for their character arcs  if they play a crucial role in defeating  her too just as they did with the demon  king this time we straight up see the  burn marks on merlin's mouth from her  kiss with escanor  proving that this is in fact after  escondor has passed away but  significantly we see esknore's the one  mode  now could this just be 